<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">21 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 21 February, from 1613 to 1972.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-romanov" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-romanov.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1613">1613 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">413 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mikhail Romanov elected Tsar of Russia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An assembly of the land chose sixteen-year-old Mikhail <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-romanov">Romanov</a> as tsar (21 February Old Style), ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/time-of-troubles">Time of Troubles</a>. His dynasty ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> until the revolution of 1917.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1804">1804 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">222 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Trevithick's steam locomotive makes the first railway journey</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Richard Trevithick's locomotive hauled ten tons of iron and some 70 men along the Penydarren tramway in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-wales">South Wales</a>. It was the first working railway journey by a steam locomotive.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1848">1848 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">178 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Marx and Engels publish 'The Communist Manifesto'</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Commissioned by the Communist League, the pamphlet appeared in German in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> just as revolution swept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. Its call 'Workers of the world, unite!' inspired socialist movements for generations.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1916">1916 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">110 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Battle of Verdun begins</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a massive bombardment, the German army attacked the French fortress city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/verdun">Verdun</a>. The battle lasted ten months and caused some 700,000 casualties, becoming a symbol of French endurance.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/german-empire">German Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-verdun">Battle of Verdun</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1965">1965 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">61 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Malcolm X assassinated in Harlem</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Malcolm X was shot dead as he began speaking at the Audubon Ballroom in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>. A year after leaving the Nation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>, he had been moving towards a broader vision of human rights.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1972">1972 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">54 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Richard Nixon arrives in Beijing</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Nixon became the first US President to visit the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-republic-of-china">People's Republic of China</a>, meeting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mao-zedong">Mao Zedong</a>. His week-long trip ended more than two decades of hostility and reshaped <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cold-war">Cold War</a> diplomacy.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-republic-of-china">People's Republic of China</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a></div></div></li></ol>
